(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// flowgraph.c's passes over a bcUnit (queue 229): the ports keep their names. The line passes and the jump threading the"] [4 1 "// compiler's flow! did (arbace/python/compile.ae) find nothing left to do; they run again for what the IR's expansion adds."] [37 1 "// bcHasTarget is HAS_TARGET without the block pushes, which are the instructions' except here."] [64 1 "// removeUnreachable is remove_unreachable; a handler is reached by the instructions it covers."] [73 2 "// remove_unreachable reaches a handler from its SETUP_* pseudo instruction, which the IR has not: a handler's"] [74 2 "// entry (PUSH_EXC_INFO) laid out after reachable code is reached, even when its region lost every instruction"] [75 2 "// (try: pass; queue 248)"] [133 1 "// removeNops is basicblock_remove_redundant_nops."] [237 1 "// propagateLineNumbers is propagate_line_numbers."] [257 4 "// 3.15 (queue 238): an empty target of one predecessor passes the location on to its next"] [279 1 "// bcConstNaN is whether o is a float or complex with a NaN part (queue 553): _PyCode_ConstantKey's key of such a constant"] [280 1 "// is (type, o), equal to another's only when it is the same object (NaN != NaN), so two NaNs folded apart stay two"] [281 1 "// constants (test_marshal's test_unorderable_set_items_in_code: {(nan)*1j, (nan)*2j, 1.5} keeps both items)."] [292 1 "// addConst is add_const: an equal constant of the same type is that one."] [315 1 "// bcLoadsConst is loads_const: 3.15's also takes LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT (queue 238)."] [320 1 "// bcCommonConst is the interpreter's common_consts[k] (pycore_opcode_utils.h's CONSTANT_*)."] [350 1 "// bcMakeLoadCommon is maybe_instr_make_load_common_const (3.15): None, True, False, \"\" and -1 as LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT."] [380 1 "// makeLoadConst is instr_make_load_const: a small int, under 3.15 a common constant, else a constant."] [397 1 "// constLoads is get_const_loading_instrs."] [424 1 "// foldTuple is fold_tuple_of_constants."] [443 1 "// foldConstantSeq is fold_constant_seq_into_load_const (3.14.10, queue 248): BUILD_LIST 0 (BUILD_SET 0), then a constant"] [444 1 "// and LIST_APPEND 1 (SET_ADD 1) alternating, i the last add or the LIST_TO_TUPLE after it: one load of a tuple (a frozenset"] [445 1 "// for a set) at i, the rest NOPs without a location (the last add too, when it is i: its load keeps no location)."] [532 1 "// bcFoldSafe is const_folding_safe_multiply, _power, _lshift and _mod."] [548 10 "// NB_MULTIPLY"] [563 10 "// NB_POWER"] [571 10 "// NB_LSHIFT"] [576 10 "// NB_REMAINDER"] [587 1 "// foldConstBinop is fold_const_binop."] [626 1 "// foldConstUnary is fold_const_unaryop."] [657 1 "// optimizeListsAndSets is optimize_lists_and_sets."] [702 1 "// optimizeLoadConst is basicblock_optimize_load_const."] [779 3 "// 3.15: what still loads a constant of the common ones is LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT"] [797 1 "// optimizeBasicBlock is optimize_basic_block, the constant folding of the expressions left to the compiler's flow!."] [921 1 "// bcSwaptimize is swaptimize; it returns the last index of the run."] [1038 1 "// removeUnusedConsts is remove_unused_consts."] [1113 1 "// addChecks is add_checks_for_loads_of_uninitialized_variables."] [1173 1 "// insertSuperinstructions is insert_superinstructions."] [1244 1 "// pushColdBlocksToEnd is push_cold_blocks_to_end."] [1288 1 "// handlerDepths finds each handler's start depth where its region starts (what SETUP_* did): the IR gives the depth to"] [1289 1 "// unwind to in its own stack, which is less than CPython's by the NULLs and selves of the region's start."] [1366 2 "// a handler whose region lost every instruction (try: pass) has no row: CPython's SETUP_* still sets its depth,"] [1367 2 "// the try statement's plus the exception (queue 248). Its entry follows reachable code, which ends at the try"] [1368 2 "// statement's depth"] [1372 4 "// the try statement's depth: the IR's after the instruction before the handler (its body's jump or return),"] [1373 4 "// with the exception; the IR's depth there is the cleanup row's (an unreached instruction's is not known)"] [1394 1 "// calculateStackdepth is calculate_stackdepth."] [1442 2 "// SETUP_*'s jump to a handler no instruction is covered by (handlerDepths' setup-reached entries; queue 248)"] [1456 1 "// insertPrefix is insert_prefix_instructions."] [1472 62 "// 3.15: codegen_enter_scope's, bcEmit"] [1494 1 "// bcAddedExcept is the handler of an instruction basicblock_addop appends to b (queue 248): it never sets i_except, so"] [1495 1 "// the slot keeps what was there: a removed instruction's handler when the block shrank (Go's slice keeps it past the"] [1496 1 "// length, as the block's array does), else nothing (calloc's NULL). A handler's entry block (PUSH_EXC_INFO first) lost"] [1497 1 "// CPython's SETUP_CLEANUP, its last instruction shifted into the slot. 3.15 passes the jump's handler."] [1499 2 "// 3.15's basicblock_addop takes the jump's handler"] [1503 2 "// a slot Go's append never wrote is the zero instruction (op 0, CACHE: never one of the block's)"] [1510 1 "// normalizeJumps is normalize_jumps."] [1526 3 "// a new block's slots were never written: neither has a handler (cfg_builder_new_block, basicblock_addop); 3.15"] [1527 3 "// gives both the jump's"] [1539 1 "// optimizeLoadFast is optimize_load_fast."] [1624 16 "// 3.15 pushes the instruction's own index"] [1627 43 "// PUSH_REF(i, NOT_LOCAL), the C's inner i"] [1641 5 "// 3.15: an opcode that consumes no inputs (the iterable stays the iterator's support)"] [1652 35 "// 3.15's END_SEND pops 3"] [1695 56 "// 3.15: BB_HAS_FALLTHROUGH, an empty block's too"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[57 18] [57 28] [67 18] [67 28] [78 19] [78 29] [111 21] [121 17] [125 18] [125 28] [137 14] [137 33] [152 45] [180 18] [180 28] [188 18] [188 28] [211 19] [211 26] [214 19] [214 29] [239 18] [239 28] [269 29] [344 69] [368 25] [383 23] [384 25] [400 6] [400 30] [459 1